# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MOASYS-Vault — Audiobooks ignore list (EXAMPLE)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A "do not warn me about this" list for your audiobooks library. Anything
# listed here is silently dropped from output/<drive>/audiobooks/warnings.json
# on every run, and counted in the run summary.
#
# Ignore lists are per DRIVE as well as per type, because warning paths are
# relative to that drive's root_path. `ignored/server/audiobooks.yaml` only
# affects runs against the root named "Server".
#
# How to use this file:
#   1. Copy it to `ignored/<drive>/audiobooks.yaml` (drop the `.example`
#      suffix). The real file is gitignored so your personal decisions stay
#      out of version control.
#   2. Add names under the level they belong to.
#   3. Re-run `npm run audiobooks <drive>`. Matching warnings disappear.
#
# ── Levels ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   folders    a category folder        - Other Audible
#   authors    one author folder        - J.R.R. Tolkien
#   books      one book                 - The Hobbit
#                                         (or  J.R.R. Tolkien/The Hobbit)
#   chapters   one file, qualified      - The Hobbit/09 - Chapter 9.mp3
#
# Names are matched at their own level and are CATEGORY-INDEPENDENT: a book
# listed here is silenced whether it sits in Audible/, Book On CD/, or both.
# That is also what lets an entry reach warn_duplicate_book, which reports
# `Author/Book` with no category to anchor to.
#
# For a multi-author book the author name is the comma-joined folder form, the
# same string the scanner reports — `Don Malarkey, Bob Welch`.
#
# ── Qualifiers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `chapters:` entries must name their book. A bare `09 - Chapter 9.mp3` exists
# in hundreds of books, so one such entry would silence all of them — the
# loader rejects it rather than let that happen quietly. `books:` may be bare
# or qualified with the author. A `/` means "somewhere above", not
# "immediately above".
#
# ── Scope ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# An entry silences EVERY warning at or below its level — chapter gaps,
# naming, unexpected entries, all of them. There is no per-warning-type
# scoping. To turn off a whole warning type instead, set
# `checks.warn_*: false` in rules/audiobooks.yaml.
#
# ── Matching ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Exact per level (not a prefix), case-insensitive, and either slash works.
#
# ── Finding names ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Take them from the `path` values in output/<drive>/audiobooks/warnings.json,
# dropping the leading category folder.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# Silence everything under a category folder
# folders:
#   - Other Audible
#   - Book On CD


# Silence a whole author
# authors:
#   - Some Author
#   - Don Malarkey, Bob Welch


# Silence one book
# (Drops every warning on it — chapter gaps, bad chapter names, unexpected
# entries. Common for a multi-part book whose numbering legitimately skips.)
# books:
#   - The Lord of the Rings
#   - J.R.R. Tolkien/The Lord of the Rings


# Silence one chapter file
# chapters:
#   - The Lord of the Rings/09 - Chapter 9.mp3
#   - J.R.R. Tolkien/The Lord of the Rings/09 - Chapter 9.mp3
